ls of the token being used by the investor to buy a ticket","userDetails":"whether the user is currently an investor and how many payment tokens is using"},"returns":{"expectedAmount":"the expected amount of tokens bought by the user"}},"getPriceInPaymentToken((address,address,address,uint24),uint256)":{"details":"Method to retrieve the price of a given token used by the user in terms of paymentToken, provided that a Uniswap v3 pool of such token against the paymentToken exists.","params":{"poolDetails":"the Uniswap v3 pool of the token used against the paymentToken","twapInterval":"what twap interval should be used"},"returns":{"price":"the price of the token used against the paymenToken with 18 decimals of precision"}},"getUSDPriceOfPaymentToken(address,uint256)":{"details":"Method to retrieve the USD price of the paymentToken through its paymentTokenOracle with 18 decimals of precision","params":{"paymentTokenOracle":"the oracle of the paymentToken to be priced","twapInterval":"what twap interval should be used"},"returns":{"_0":"the USD price of the paymenToken in USD with 18 decimals of precision"}},"resetAllowances(address,address,address[])":{"details":"Method to reset all allowances in case the Uniswap router must be changed in the escrow contract","params":{"newAddress":"the new Uniswap router","oldAddress":"the old Uniswap router","tokensERC20":"the list of tokens whose allowances must be reset"}},"setAllowed(address,bool)":{"details":"Method restricted in access to be called by the factory to allow/disallow specific escrows from calling this contract","params":{"status":"whether to allow it or not","toBeSet":"the address of the escrow to allow/disallow"}},"swapTokensForPaymentTokens((address,address,address,uint24),uint256,uint256)":{"details":"Method to swap a given token for paymentToken using an existing Uniswap v3 pool","params":{"expectedAmount":"the expected amount of paymentToken to control slippage","poolDetails":"the Uniswap v3 pool of the token used against the paymentToken","tokenAmount":"the amount of tokens being swapped"}}},"title":"PriceAndSwapManager: contract that handles logic for the STOEscrowUpgradeable contract. Due to contract size limit we had to hand off this into a separate contract. It abstracts away price recovery and swap logic. It supports Uniswap v3 pools and Chainlink price feeds. This is a stateless, non upgradeable contract that is deployed once for every chain and to which all escrows will need to point to.  If this needs to change, the factory has methods to change it accordingly to a newly deployed one.","version":1},"userdoc":{"errors":{"NotNegativeValue(int256)":[{"notice":"The value is negative"}],"NotZeroAddress()":[{"notice":"The Address can't be zero address"}],"UserIsNotAdmin(address)":[{"notice":"User `user`,don't have permission to reinitialize the contract"}],"UserIsNotWhitelisted(address)":[{"notice":"User is not Whitelisted, User `user`,don't have permission to transfer or call some functions"}],"WrongUniswapConfig()":[{"notice":"When something is wrong with Uniswap config"}]},"kind":"user","methods":{},"version":1}},"settings":{"compilationTarget":{"contracts/sto/helpers/PriceAndSwapManager.sol":"PriceAndSwapManager"},"evmVersion":"cancun","libraries":{},"metadata":{"bytecodeHash":"ipfs"},"optimizer":{"enabled":true,"runs":100},"remappings":[":@ensdomains/=node_modules/@ensdomains/",":@openzeppelin/contracts-upgradeable/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts-upgradeable/contracts/",":@openzeppelin/contracts/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/contracts/",":ds-test/=lib/ethereum-vault-connector/lib/forge-std/lib/ds-test/src/",":dto/escrow/=contracts/dto/escrow/",":dto/factory/=contracts/dto/factory/",":dto/helpers/=contracts/dto/helpers/",":dto/interfaces/=contracts/dto/interfaces/",":dto/mocks/=contracts/dto/mocks/",":dto/token/=contracts/dto/token/",":erc4626-tests/=lib/openzeppelin-contracts/lib/erc4626-tests/",":eth-gas-reporter/=node_modules/eth-gas-reporter/",":ethereum-vault-conne